{
  "$comment": "Policy for scripts/quality/audit_qt_usage.py (gate G13). Ceilings may only fall: lower them in the commit that removes Qt (audit_qt_usage.py --print-ceilings).",
  "scan_root": "src/libs/mne",
  "exclude_path_fragments": {
    "/FormFiles/": "Qt Designer generated forms (uic input); not hand-maintained C++.",
    "_autogen/": "moc/uic/rcc output; generated at build time."
  },
  "qt_by_design": [
    "disp",
    "disp3D"
  ],
  "kept": {
    "$comment": "Library -> { use: reason } for Qt kept by decision D16.",
    "disp": {
      "SvgWriter (QPaintEngine)": "Replaces QSvgGenerator so the vector export of widgets needs Qt Gui only; dropping the Qt Svg module raised the disp ceilings once (tokens 6025 -> 6159, public header includes 110 -> 112).",
      "QWindow hosts and scene viewports (phase 3)": "ChannelWindow (QWindow + QRhi swap chain) next to the ChannelRhiView QRhiWidget host, and SceneViewport replacing the QGraphicsView scenes, raised the disp ceilings once (tokens 4846 -> 4885, public header includes 82 -> 89); the QRhiWidget hosts go with phase 4.",
      "Qt input translation shared with the brain view": "toScenePointerEvent() and toSceneWheelEvent() (plots/helpers/sceneinput.h), which ChannelRhiRenderer and disp3D's BrainViewCore share instead of each translating Qt events, raised the disp ceilings once (tokens 4543 -> 4549); the brain view's camera, input, layout and overlay moving to mne_scene lowered disp3D from 1961 to 1807 tokens.",
      "QRhi backend of the GPU frame description": "RhiFrameRenderer (plots/helpers/rhiframerenderer.h) executes the Qt-free scene::GpuFrame of any view with QRhi: pipelines, buffers, textures and shader reflection checks in one place instead of in each renderer. ChannelRhiRenderer lost its own QRhi code to it, net raising the disp ceilings once (tokens 4529 -> 4546); the brain view moving onto it lowers disp3D.",
      "Generic settings panel builder": "SettingsPanel (viewers/settingspanel.h) builds the Qt Widgets of any Qt-free scene::SettingsForm, so a new toolkit needs one builder instead of a hand-written view per panel; the builder raised the disp ceilings once (tokens 4546 -> 4601); the covariance, spectrum, averaging, filter, artifact and time-frequency settings views ported onto it lowered them again (tokens 4601 -> 4519)."
    },
    "disp3D": {
      "BrainWindow host and GPU overlay (phase 3)": "BrainWindow (QWindow + QRhi swap chain), the forwarding BrainView host and the overlay painted into the GPU pass instead of child QLabels raised the disp3D ceilings once (tokens 1633 -> 1961); the QRhiWidget host goes with phase 4."
    }
  },
